    isbefore: []  # 2e6b
    duplicate_of: []  # 2e6b
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2e6b
    pr_ref:  # 2e6b
    description: "FOUND while merging PR #585 (WI-gibom). auto-pr printed \"Attaching git note with original\ncommit body...\" and then, twice, a red BLOCKED banner listing 565 commits all titled\n\"Notes added by 'git notes add'\". auto-pr still exited 0.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. .githooks/pre-push loops over every stdin ref line. The protected-branch\ncheck strips refs/heads/ and compares, so it is a no-op for a notes ref -- but the DCO\ncheck that follows has NO ref-kind guard at all. It runs `git rev-list --no-merges` over\nwhatever is being pushed and demands a Signed-off-by trailer on each commit. Commits on\nrefs/notes/commits are generated by `git notes add`; they carry the fixed auto-generated\nsubject \"Notes added by 'git notes add'\" and no trailer, and there is no way to add one.\nSo the notes ref is unpushable by construction while this hook is installed.\n\nMEASURED, not inferred:\n  git ls-remote origin 'refs/notes/*'   -> EMPTY. The ref does not exist on origin at all.\n  git log --oneline refs/notes/commits | wc -l   -> 565\n  oldest 2026-01-22, newest 2026-08-27 (today)\nSo every note written since the notes mechanism was introduced lives in exactly one\nworking copy and has never been replicated.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS RATHER THAN BEING COSMETIC:\n  1. AGENTS.md \"Merge Strategy\" offers --squash as a fallback and says it \"Preserves body\n     via git notes\". That preservation is LOCAL ONLY. A squash-merged commit's original\n     body is recoverable from this machine and nowhere else.\n  2. AGENTS.md \"Git Notes\" instructs a reader to run\n     `git fetch origin refs/notes/*:refs/notes/*`. That command fetches nothing, because\n     the ref is absent on origin. The documented recovery path does not work.\n  3. The bodies of the Jan 9-22 2026 historical commits were deliberately restored via\n     notes. A fresh clone does not get them. This is a single-point-of-failure for content\n     the project spent effort preserving.\n  4. IT FAILS SILENTLY. auto-pr exits 0 and reports a successful merge. Nothing downstream\n     of the note-attach step checks whether the push landed.\n\nTHE FIX IS TWO LINES AND I HAVE NOT WRITTEN IT: skip the DCO block when remote_ref does\nnot start with refs/heads/ (or specifically exempt refs/notes/), which is the same shape\nas the protected-branch check immediately above it. .githooks/** is a governance path, so\nper AGENTS.md this is filed for approval rather than PR'd.\n\nOPEN QUESTION FOR THE HUMAN, because the answer changes the fix: should the 565 existing\nnotes be pushed once approved? They are 7 months of accumulated bodies. Pushing them is a\none-time `git push origin refs/notes/*` and is additive, but it publishes commit bodies\nthat have so far only ever been local.\n\nNOT INVESTIGATED: whether the woodpecker per-PR DCO gate this hook mirrors would also\nreject a notes-ref push server-side. The hook never lets a push get that far, so the\nserver behaviour is unobserved."  # 2e6b
    fields:  # 2e6b
      statement: "A git note attached by auto-pr to preserve an original commit body is never replicated: .githooks/pre-push applies its DCO Signed-off-by check to every ref including refs/notes/commits, whose commits are auto-generated by git notes add and cannot carry a trailer, so the push is blocked; origin has no refs/notes/* at all and all 565 notes since 2026-01-22 exist only in one working copy. auto-pr exits 0 regardless."  # 2e6b
      root_cause: "The DCO block in .githooks/pre-push has no ref-kind guard. The protected-branch check above it strips refs/heads/ and is harmlessly inert on a notes ref, but the DCO check runs git rev-list over whatever ref is pushed and demands a trailer no git-notes commit can have."  # 2e6b
